    style: NATS_style.json,
    styleoverride: {
        laneWidthRel: [ 1.0,  1.0],
        lanes: 2,
        borderbottom: 45,
        titleFontSize: 11,
        bullets: false,
        bodyLineSpacingRel: 0.15,



    },
    "pageHeader": "CLI Cheatsheet - New Features",
    "pageFooter": "**Created by Synadia, the team behind NATS - www.synadia.com**   *https://github.com/roeschter/cheat-sheet-nats-synadia*",


    "blocks": [
        {
            "title": "**Overview**",
            "items": [
                "Since Nats-server v2.12, 2.14 and 2.15 a number of features have been added.",
                "Some have not (yet) been added to the standard API but are published as ***orbit extensions***.",
                {
                    bullets: true,
                    "items": [
                        "*https://github.com/synadia-io/orbit.go*",
                        "*https://github.com/synadia-io/orbit.java*",
                        "*https://github.com/synadia-io/orbit.net*",
                        "*https://github.com/synadia-io/orbit.js*",
                        "*https://github.com/synadia-io/orbit.rs*",
                        "*https://github.com/synadia-io/orbit.c*",

                    ]
                },
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "**New stream capabilities**",
            "items": [
                "See usage detailed examples in the following sections.",
            ]
        },
        {
            "items": [
                "**Per-Message TTL** - Allows for auto cleaning caches and auto removal of delete markers in KVs.",
                "``**nats s add S1 --defaults --subjects S1 --allow-msg-ttl**``",
            ]
        },
        {
            "items": [
                "**Atomic Counters** in KV stores. Works across sources",
                "``**nats s add S2 --defaults --subjects S2 --allow-counter**``",
            ]
        },
        {
            "items": [
                "**Scheduled messages** - Send messages with delay or on a repeated schedule",
                "``**nats s add S3 --defaults --subjects S3.\\* --allow-schedules --allow-msg-ttl**``",
            ]
        },
        {
            "items": [
                "**Atomic batch** - Commit a message batch to a stream atomically. Batch size is limited",
                "``**nats s add S4 --defaults --subjects S4 --allow-batch**``",
            ]
        },
        {
            "items": [
                "**Fast batch** - Send messages in guaranteed sequence without waiting for individual acks.",
                "``**nats s add S5 --replicas=3 --defaults --subjects S5 --allow-fast**``",
            ]
        },
        {
            "items": [
                "**Warning:** Only activate features on streams when you intend to use them.",
                {
                    bullets: true,
                    "items": [
                        "Some capabilities cannot be disabled once enabled (e.g. schedules)",
                        "Some capabilities are incompatible with Key Value Store or Source and Mirror (e.g. schedules)",
                    ]
                },
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "**Message TTL**",
            "items": [
                "Publish a message with different TTLs - see them disappear",
                "``**nats pub S1 Hi --header=Nats-TTL:5s**``",
                "``**nats pub S1 Hi --header=Nats-TTL:10s**``",
                "``**nats pub S1 Hi --header=Nats-TTL:15s**``",
                "``**watch -n 1 'nats s info S1**``'"
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "**Atomic Counters**",
            "items": [
                "Count (add) to a value atomically. Works on regular streams as well as KVs.",
                "``**nats request S2 '' --header=Nats-Incr:+1**``",
                "``**nats request S2 '' --header=Nats-Incr:+2**``",
                "``**nats stream get S2 --last-for=S2**``'"
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "**Scheduled Messages**",
            "items": [
                "Schedule messages to be sent later.",
                {
                    bullets: true,
                    "items": [
                        "All scheduling happens in the same stream.",
                        "The schedule lives in ***unique*** subject it is sent on. The schedule can be deleted, overwritten etc.",
                        "The message is send to ``**--schedule-dest=SUBJECT**``",
                        "The schedule may copy the last message from``**--schedule-source=SUBJECT**``",
                    ]
                },
            ]
        },
        {
            "items": [
                "Schedule **once** with delay.",
                "``**nats pub S3.1 Hi --schedule-dest=S3.s1 --schedule-at=\"$(date -d '+10 seconds' -Iseconds)\"**``",
                "``**nats stream get S3 --last-for=S3.s1**``'",
            ]
        },
        {
            "items": [
                "Scheduled message has a TTL.",
                "``**nats pub S3.2 Hi --schedule-ttl=10s --schedule-dest=S3.s2 --schedule-at=\"$(date -d '+10 seconds' -Iseconds)\"**``",
                "``**nats stream get S3 --last-for=S3.s2**``'",
            ]
        },
        {
            "items": [
               "Schedule ``**cron**`` style",
                "``**nats pub S3.3 Hi --schedule-dest=S3.s3 --schedule-cron='\\*/5 \\* \\* \\* \\* \\*'**``",
                "``**nats stream get S3 --last-for=S3.s3**``'",
            ]
        },
        {
            "items": [
                "Schedule last message from subject",
                "``**nats pub S3.template Hello**``'",
                "``**nats pub S3.4 Hi --schedule-dest=S3.s4 --schedule-cron='\\*/5 \\* \\* \\* \\* \\*' --schedule-source=S3.template**``",
                "``**nats stream get S3 --last-for=S3.s4**``'",
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "**Atomic Batch Publish**",
            "items": [
                "Publish multiple messages in one atomic, all or nothing, operation. Limited to the same stream.",
                "``**echo -e 'A\\nB\\nC\\n' | nats pub --atomic --send-on=newline S4**``",
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "**Fast Batch Publish**",
            "items": [
                "Allows safe (no dups, no messages lost) fast publishing in order.",
                "``**nats bench js pub fast S5 --stream S5**``",
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "**Stream I/O buffer optimizations**",
            "items": [
                "Replicated streams do NOT flush their buffers to disk immediately, but rather with a delay or when `sync_interval` triggers. With todays server and OS reliability in memory replication is sufficient guarantee for data persistence over a few seconds interval.",
                "Non replicated stream will flush to disk by default. If performance wins over data consistency replicas=1 streams can be set to async mode",
                "``**nats s add S6 --replicas=1 --defaults --subjects S6 --persist-mode=async**``",

            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "**Check stream downgrade compatibility**",
            "items": [
                "Check the compatibility of streams against past Jetstream API levels. Depends on the features actually activated. The command below will show the required API level of all streams.",
                "``**nats server report downgrade 0**``",

            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "**Consumer pause, resume and reset**",
            "items": [
                "Consumers can now be paused (for an amount of time), resumed or reset to their ack floor or a sequence number.",
                "``**nats consumer create S1 C1 --defaults --pull**``",
                "``**nats consumer pause S1 C1 10s**``",
                "``**nats consumer resume S1 C1**``",
                "Without ``**--sequence**`` reset rewinds to the ack floor and redelivers unacknowledged messages. Consumers with a start sequence or start time cannot be reset below it. But you can set a future one, skipping messages for a while.",
                "``**nats consumer reset S1 C1**``",
                "``**nats consumer reset S1 C1 --sequence=42**``",
                "E.g. you can now pause a stuck consumer, find the sequence number of the message it fails to process and then skip over it.",

            ]
        },
         {
            "title": "**Source/Mirror with durable consumers**",
            "items": [
                "Previously source/mirror relied on ephemeral consumers to initiate message transport, with replication state stored on the mirror stream only.",
                "Ephemeral consumers do not work as intended on interest and workqueue streams and do not allow control to the operator controlling the stream from which messages originate.",
                "2.14 now supports a new flow_control consumer which can be explicitly configured to be used with source and mirror streams.",
                "Create Origin stream with a durable consumer. The consumer is a push consumer, so we need to set a delivery subject.",
                "``**nats s add S_ORIGIN --defaults --subjects S_ORIGIN**``",
                "``**nats consumer create --defaults --ack=flow_control --heartbeat=1s --deliver=all S_ORIGIN C_MIRROR --target mirror.S_ORIGIN.C_MIRROR**``",
                "Create stream. Mirror config accepts a JSON fragment. The permutation of configuration options have become too complex to support as command line parameters.",
                "``**nats s create S_MIRROR --defaults --mirror='{\"name\":\"S_ORIGIN\",\"consumer\":{\"name\":\"C_MIRROR\",\"deliver_subject\":\"mirror.S_ORIGIN.C_MIRROR\"}}'**``",
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "**Meta cluster rescue (2.15)**",
            "items": [
                "If a cluster permanently loses the majority of its servers, the meta RAFT group cannot elect a leader and JetStream stops. ``**peer-remove**`` needs a meta leader too. Rescue temporarily lowers the quorum on the surviving servers. (SYS)",
                "Discover - the report shows ***No cluster meta leader found*** and servers missing from the RAFT Meta Group.",
                "``**nats server report jetstream**``",
                "Rescue - shows the cluster state and prompts for the new quorum size (default: servers online). Specify the domain if the servers run in one.",
                "``**nats server cluster rescue --js-domain <domain>**``",
                "The lowered quorum expires after **5 minutes**. The report shows ``**Rescuing true**``. Peer remove the dead servers within that window.",
                "``**nats server cluster peer-remove <server> --js-domain <domain>**``",
                {
                    bullets: true,
                    "items": [
                        "Only for servers that will never come back. **Use with caution**",
                        "Survivors must hold data - servers with an empty log refuse the rescue",
                    ]
                },
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "**Backup - new format (2.15)**",
            "items": [
                "``**nats backup**`` replaces ``**nats stream backup**`` and ``**nats account backup**``. The new format can be inspected, validated and **edited offline**. Requires server 2.15+.",
                "``**nats backup stream ORDERS ./bk**``",
                "``**nats backup account ./bk_all**``",
                "``**nats backup info ./bk --subjects**``",
                "``**nats backup validate ./bk**``",
                "``**nats backup restore stream ./bk**``",
            ]
        },
        {
            "items": [
                "**Edit** writes a filtered copy of a backup. Filter by subject, time, sequence, header or payload. Preview with ``**--dry-run**``.",
                "``**nats backup edit ./bk ./bk2 --exclude-subject=orders.test --exclude-payload-match=card --dry-run**``",
                "Keep the last 2 hours and renumber from 1 (drops consumers)",
                "``**nats backup edit ./bk ./bk2 --after=2h --renumber**``",
                "Compact a KV backup - latest revision per key, deleted keys dropped",
                "``**nats backup edit ./kv ./kv2 --kv-compact**``",
                "Obfuscate before sharing, e.g. with support. Keep the key file private.",
                "``**nats backup edit ./bk ./bk_obf --obfuscate**``",
                "``**nats backup lookup ./bk_obf.keys.json <value>**``",
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "**Default consumer limit (2.15)**",
            "items": [
                "Streams are now limited to **1000 consumers** unless ``**max_consumers**`` is set on the stream or in the account limits. Existing consumers are kept, but new ones fail with ***maximum consumers limit reached (10026)***.",
                "**Warning:** ``**nats s info**`` still shows ***Maximum Consumers: unlimited***.",
                "Raise the limit per stream",
                "``**nats s add S7 --defaults --subjects S7 --max-consumers=5000**``",
                "``**nats s edit S7 --max-consumers=5000**``",
                "Or change the server-wide default in the server config (-1 = unlimited)",
                "``**jetstream { limits { default_max_consumers: 5000 } }**``",
            ]
        },
    ]
}